  "seoBody": "<p>You inspect sites in Ireland. Your Records hold personal and work data. This page says where Quickler keeps it.</p><h2>On EU servers</h2><p>Your Records and photos sit on EU servers in Germany, run on Hetzner. One clear path: WhatsApp in, report out. Quickler works anywhere WhatsApp works.</p><h2>The rules you already know</h2><p>GDPR applies in Ireland through the Data Protection Act 2018. The Data Protection Commission oversees it. Quickler is built to follow GDPR and keep data in the EU. This is not legal advice. You still choose your own lawful basis, how long you keep data and who sees it.</p><h2>Why a Record beats paper</h2><h3>Built while you work</h3><p>Every answer, photo and voice note goes into one Record as you send it. You do not write it up from memory.</p><h3>Each Fault has a place</h3><p>Faults are listed with where they are. Each one becomes a job, a To do.</p><h3>Word, PDF or a link</h3><p>Get your report as Word, PDF or a web link. The Record behind it stays in one place.</p><h2>Questions from Irish firms</h2><h3>Where is the data stored?</h3><p>On EU servers in Germany, run on Hetzner. Your Records and photos stay inside the European Union.</p><h3>Does Quickler follow GDPR in Ireland?</h3><p>Quickler is built to follow GDPR, which applies in Ireland under the Data Protection Act 2018. This is not legal advice. Check your own duties with your adviser.</p><h3>Do I install a new app?</h3><p>No. You answer in WhatsApp on the phone you already have, by text, voice note or photo. You pay £75 a month for each phone number on the account. See our <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">overview</a>.</p><h3>Can it fill in my own report?</h3><p>Yes. Send a finished report in Word or PDF. Every new report comes back in that layout, with your headings, tables and logo. Browse the <a href=\"/pages/services.html\">Checks</a> to see the range.</p>",
